Upstream LMCache PR #5116, package files only.

    https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/pull/5116
    "[fix][mp] keep the server's exported completion event alive (ROCm 10.0)"
    OPEN as of 2026-09-15, author sammshen.

Supersedes 0001-retain-exported-ipc-events.patch, which fixes the same bug one
layer down. Do NOT apply both: 0001 retains a bounded ring of up to 4096
exported events in the event backend; #5116 removes the need to retain anything
by giving each registered context a single long-lived completion_event that is
re-recorded and re-exported per transfer. That also drops a per-transfer
interprocess event allocation on the offload hot path.

Fetched with `gh pr diff 5116` and filtered to lmcache/ -- the PR also carries
docs/ and tests/, which the installed package does not have, so an unfiltered
apply fails with "can't find file to patch".

Verified to apply cleanly to lmcache 0.5.6.dev3+rocm7.2 on 2026-09-15.
Delete this file once #5116 merges and reaches the AMD nightly.

